<PageLayout lang="en" title="About PayCards" heading="About PayCards" description="PayCards is an independent guide to the RedotPay card. The English pages quote official sources and name the PayCards team, not a personal author." page="about-en" path="/en/about">
  <p><strong>PayCards</strong> explains how a RedotPay card works in ordinary spending: online checkout, phone wallets, and ATM cash. The Arabic site is the original. These English pages cover the same product for readers searching in English.</p>
  <p>We are not RedotPay. Signup always happens on RedotPay’s own site.</p>
  <h2>Who writes</h2>
  <p>The byline is the <strong>PayCards team</strong>. We do not invent a personal author, and we do not publish reviews, ratings, or user stories we did not document. If a line is wrong, email us.</p>
  <h2>How we check facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>RedotPay figures — fees, the sign-up reward, country lists, card programmes — come from RedotPay’s help center or redotpay.com. The source is linked under the table or in the guide.</li>
    <li>Each numbers page shows the date <strong>we checked</strong> it, and the date on RedotPay’s page when that date is visible. If the app has changed since then, the amount shown before you confirm is the one that counts.</li>
    <li>If we cannot find a fixed number, we do not guess. We say the figure is in the app, or that it was not on the pages we read.</li>
    <li>An article’s “updated” date changes only when that article changes.</li>
    <li>Some links are referral links. That does not change your fee. See the <a href="/en/disclosure">disclosure</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What we will not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Call the card Mastercard. The card terms we read name Visa for the Hong Kong and Singapore programmes, and newer help pages say “major card networks”.</li>
    <li>Publish a competitor’s fees we did not check on the same day.</li>
    <li>Treat a missing country as permission to use the card.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>A limit you should read</h2>
  <p>Crypto prices move, and this site is not financial, investment, or legal advice. The English pages are for readers outside the United States: RedotPay does not issue a card to US residents, and the app does not open if you are located there. Other countries are blocked too. Read the <a href="/en/articles/redotpay-supported-countries">country lists</a> and the app before you pay an issuance fee.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Corrections and topic ideas: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  <CTABox lang="en" position="end" />
</PageLayout>
